# Served by Workers Static Assets for every non-API path — the Worker never
# runs for those (`run_worker_first = ["/api/*"]`), so its middleware cannot
# set them. The policy is what the built client actually needs and nothing
# more: no inline scripts (Vite emits none), inline *style attributes* only
# (React's `style={{…}}` on the sheet drag, the scrim and the skeletons),
# images from this origin plus the `blob:` URL the preview map is drawn from,
# fetches to this origin only. Maps open in a new tab, which CSP does not govern.
#
# The one third party: Cloudflare Web Analytics, which the zone injects into
# every HTML response as `<script defer src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js">`
# and which reports to `cloudflareinsights.com`. Named explicitly rather than
# widened to a wildcard — the first deploy of this file blocked it and the
# console said so on every page.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
